codex
Concrete execution now returns exactly `[]` and `["a","ab","abc"]`. I’m tightening the symbolic layer so its loop summary is backed by a separate inductive claim, using an abstract prefix accumulator that normalizes one loop iteration in constant time; this avoids the prover eagerly expanding an unbounded recursive list.
